#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128835 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129259 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08375770-c610-5dae-b01b-c457de086cba" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rule and Swap Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "d180f745-028b-5859-8cad-4a49b5c20773" :question/math-academy-id "e-10521" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{15} \\sum_{j=1}^{18} (a_{i} - 2)( b_{j}+1)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{15}a_i = 40, \\qquad \\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^{18}b_j =-8 .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n  a_{i}b_j = \\sum_{i=1}^m a_i \\sum_{j=1}^n b_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}({a}_{i}-2)({b}_{j}+1) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}({b}_{j}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}({b}_{j}+1) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}2)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}{b}_{j}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}1) \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}-2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}1)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}{b}_{j}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{18}1) \\\\  & =(40-2\\cdot 15)\\cdot (-8+18) \\\\  & =(10)\\cdot (10) \\\\  & =100.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128992 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129173 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8537cc22-8d18-57c8-9ebf-921bd4d06ae7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Summation"}] :question/id #uuid "e17f982d-3d3e-5279-b507-d390e4f1970f" :question/math-academy-id "e-6116" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^3\\sum_{i=1}^2 (i+j).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(i+j) & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(i+j)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}[(1+j)+(2+j)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(3+2j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the sum above by summing over the index $j\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(3+2j) & =(3+2\\cdot 1)+(3+2\\cdot 2)+(3+2\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =5+7+9 \\\\  & =21\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128993 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129174 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4312c28-e298-5185-9009-e6ca243175fd" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "e8f3608f-68f2-5ba9-b618-447887e7f6fb" :question/math-academy-id "e-6118" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} (1+2a_{ij}-b_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8}  a_{ij} = 8, \\qquad\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8}  b_{ij} = 15.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}(1+2{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}2{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+2(8)-15 \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n 1 = mn,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{8}1)+1 & =5\\cdot 8+1 \\\\  & =40+1 \\\\  & =41.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^{5} \\sum_{j=1}^{8} (1+2a_{ij}-b_{ij}) = 41.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129174 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4312c28-e298-5185-9009-e6ca243175fd" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d2b29b9-329a-5455-8348-aa7f4fcfe8f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "400" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416650} {:answer/id #uuid "a91e6846-0988-53c3-b781-324cbc6a73d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "800" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416651} {:answer/id #uuid "b40a38f1-fed4-5c13-82e8-1d517cf82331" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "260" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416652} {:answer/id #uuid "c78c8f9f-8af1-5372-9268-aae2ae1ac714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,600" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416653} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2b240a-91ea-5638-a32d-6d16bc129b5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "220" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d2b29b9-329a-5455-8348-aa7f4fcfe8f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "400" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416650} :answer-field/id #uuid "82c98e1b-2b7a-5bde-9360-7f012814c1b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416655}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d34efdb1-67e3-5372-9a9f-94c6cc6bc5be" :question/math-academy-id "q-149600" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}4({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}{a}_{ij}=40,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}{b}_{ij}=60.\n$$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying these rules to the given sum, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}4({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & =4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) \\\\  & =4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}{a}_{ij}+4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{50}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{100}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 40+4\\cdot 60 \\\\  & =160+240 \\\\  & =400.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275228 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129174 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4312c28-e298-5185-9009-e6ca243175fd" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f564799-072a-59cc-96e5-da621926444a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272663} {:answer/id #uuid "30d49607-ca61-5e6a-9a58-381e5e653ae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272821} {:answer/id #uuid "b241ab01-5e9b-57e2-b39d-41a0df962b2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273928} {:answer/id #uuid "d649f46b-6f36-5773-9cfd-5caf55c72157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274262} {:answer/id #uuid "fb661a82-596b-553a-8787-25455a66aa3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b241ab01-5e9b-57e2-b39d-41a0df962b2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273928} :answer-field/id #uuid "3837bfb6-67dd-5e82-82e3-c2662a455ffd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f734ef27-c15e-5fba-9fca-e94f9a86d030" :question/math-academy-id "q-149676" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}-2)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}{a}_{ij}=300,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}{b}_{ij}=250.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}-2) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}{b}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}2 \\\\  & =300+250-(2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}1) \\\\  & =550-2({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}1=mn,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}550-2({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}1) & =550-2\\cdot (15\\cdot 16) \\\\  & =550-480 \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{16}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}-2)=70.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129259 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08375770-c610-5dae-b01b-c457de086cba" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rule and Swap Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2b739c5-c8b2-5d66-bd15-ef2f8e39e22f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "290" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371867} {:answer/id #uuid "1ac2df96-9c6b-5f86-8982-4c6f89455e73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "270" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371868} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ae4afc-a713-5930-a923-062a26b12166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "330" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371869} {:answer/id #uuid "6ae4e75b-9802-500c-992c-40e97c52da56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "310" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371870} {:answer/id #uuid "9c97ebb1-e16a-55a1-ae0c-fae857b30213" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "250" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ac2df96-9c6b-5f86-8982-4c6f89455e73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "270" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371868} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a9613f8-bb30-5421-9518-35d93e8b06bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371866}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9cefe9ad-c8c4-50df-9dcf-62888d4bac69" :question/math-academy-id "q-149725" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}3{a}_{i}(4-{b}_{j})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}=30,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}{b}_{j}=45.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}3{a}_{i}(4-{b}_{j}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}3{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}(4-{b}_{j}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}3{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}(4-{b}_{j}) & =(3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}4-{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}{b}_{j}) \\\\  & =(3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i})\\cdot (4{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}1-{\\sum }_{j=1}^{12}{b}_{j}) \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 30)\\cdot (4\\cdot 12-45) \\\\  & =(90)\\cdot (48-45) \\\\  & =(90)\\cdot (3) \\\\  & =270\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365136 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129259 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08375770-c610-5dae-b01b-c457de086cba" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rule and Swap Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "739f02b8-1a50-51f3-b599-b2d4bbdcbbfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365138} {:answer/id #uuid "66ac2e80-2f19-533a-a54c-aaae64ac9ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365139} {:answer/id #uuid "1a545440-ad2d-5415-9818-1f826b19a3c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365140} {:answer/id #uuid "157f184b-3e0c-5861-b6d4-bada121dbff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365141} {:answer/id #uuid "94b49b2d-2250-5680-ac10-074346d4a0fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94b49b2d-2250-5680-ac10-074346d4a0fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365142} :answer-field/id #uuid "b944858b-8baa-5d16-beac-cfb6cb20defd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365137}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "50f28902-c131-5862-a511-9c9ad13508fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-149738" :question/problem "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}({a}_{i}-2)({b}_{j}-5)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{a}_{i}=35,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}{b}_{j}=70.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}({a}_{i}-2)({b}_{j}-5) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}({b}_{j}-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}({a}_{i}-2){\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}({b}_{j}-5) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{a}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}2)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}{b}_{j}-{\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}5) \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{a}_{i}-2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}1)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}{b}_{j}-5{\\sum }_{j=1}^{13}1) \\\\  & =(35-2\\cdot 10)\\cdot (70-5\\cdot 13) \\\\  & =(35-20)\\cdot (70-65) \\\\  & =(15)\\cdot (5) \\\\  & =75.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129850 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129173 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8537cc22-8d18-57c8-9ebf-921bd4d06ae7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Summation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ee3daa0-63ea-57fd-8203-29e8ffd77480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336174} {:answer/id #uuid "12b2522f-4758-5d90-8080-b542234b7547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336210} {:answer/id #uuid "39fbd0e6-1e9a-5d05-a795-60d8cfddca47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336577} {:answer/id #uuid "d237224f-7536-5f2e-8a8f-f0e65701610b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337874} {:answer/id #uuid "f10ed6bc-4030-5ec3-a3e8-ed644aee61ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39fbd0e6-1e9a-5d05-a795-60d8cfddca47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336577} :answer-field/id #uuid "58439c8e-2c44-5252-9a32-9e790d2edd09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338427}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e16a192-c647-58f3-9bd2-bc5597aebc2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-72094" :question/problem "${\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}ij=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}ij & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}ij] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}(1j+2j+3j) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}(j+2j+3j) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}6j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we sum over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}6j & =6\\cdot 1+6\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6+12 \\\\  & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339105 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129173 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8537cc22-8d18-57c8-9ebf-921bd4d06ae7" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Summation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0735a4cd-515a-5587-aec7-e76fddc755c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336086} {:answer/id #uuid "55d93502-79ac-5c15-ae2a-e1112695e68e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336820} {:answer/id #uuid "86c72bf0-c408-5bb8-9e5f-5051a72af735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337251} {:answer/id #uuid "8f7018cc-6c17-5066-b6ad-719333adc2ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337328} {:answer/id #uuid "eb671908-d81f-5a98-9906-00407e93a199" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0735a4cd-515a-5587-aec7-e76fddc755c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336086} :answer-field/id #uuid "d00b4e5a-ff65-56fa-b540-8141b99bade6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84a0ce9f-42da-567f-9eb4-191f3ceeaf0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-72398" :question/problem "${\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}\\frac{i}{j}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}\\frac{i}{j} & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}[{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}\\frac{i}{j}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}(\\frac{1}{j}+\\frac{2}{j}+\\frac{3}{j}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}\\frac{6}{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we sum over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}\\frac{6}{j} & =\\frac{6}{1}+\\frac{6}{2}+\\frac{6}{3} \\\\  & =6+3+2 \\\\  & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
